        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/authentication-role-routing-and-entry-point-mapping",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Authentication, role routing, and entry-point mapping — Ruled out: Flutter routes, AuthGate, AppShell, and feature modules\n\nClient-side route arguments can be forged, but every privileged backend path is independently enforced before the sink: profile roles are immutable to authenticated clients via column grants, editor/teacher checks bind to `auth.uid()`, and table/RPC mutations are constrained by RLS or role-checked SECURITY DEFINER functions. No route-only privilege escalation reaches protected data/state."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Flutter routes, AuthGate, AppShell, and feature modules"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Authentication, role routing, and entry-point mapping",
              "surface": "Flutter routes, AuthGate, AppShell, and feature modules",
              "recorded_by": "Repository Mapping Lead",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/data-authorization-idor-privileged-rpc-mapping",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Data authorization / IDOR / privileged RPC mapping — No issue identified: Supabase schema, RLS policies, SECURITY DEFINER functions, and client repository call sites\n\nCompleted policy/function review: all 21 application tables have RLS, all 58 policies were traced, and every SECURITY DEFINER function has `search_path=''`, caller/role/relationship checks or trigger-only reachability, plus explicit public/anon revokes. Dart mutations/RPCs rely on these controls; no complete authorization bypass trace was found."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Supabase schema, RLS policies, SECURITY DEFINER functions, and client repository call sites"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "no_issue_found",
              "risk_area": "Data authorization / IDOR / privileged RPC mapping",
              "surface": "Supabase schema, RLS policies, SECURITY DEFINER functions, and client repository call sites",
              "recorded_by": "Repository Mapping Lead",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/file-upload-private-object-authorization-path-handling-and-elevated-service-access",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "File upload, private-object authorization, path handling, and elevated-service access — Ruled out: Private media flow: file picker, validators, Supabase Storage policies, and get-private-media Edge Function\n\nStatic trace confirms private-media access is fail-closed: the Edge Function validates the bearer with `auth.getUser`, resolves records through the caller's RLS client, checks owner/assigned-teacher/editor/publication state, validates path shape, then uses the service key only for the already-authorized exact object. Storage policies independently bind bucket, operation, role/owner, record, and path."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Private media flow: file picker, validators, Supabase Storage policies, and get-private-media Edge Function"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "File upload, private-object authorization, path handling, and elevated-service access",
              "surface": "Private media flow: file picker, validators, Supabase Storage policies, and get-private-media Edge Function",
              "recorded_by": "Repository Mapping Lead",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/automated-sast-and-structural-source-mapping",
          "ruleIndex": 4,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Automated SAST and structural source mapping — No issue identified: Scoped Semgrep and AST-grep structural pass over product source\n\nSemgrep scanned 78 runtime/config files with `p/default` and `p/secrets`, producing 0 findings and 0 engine errors. `sg-targets.txt` was derived from Semgrep `paths.scanned`, and a bounded `$F($$$ARGS)` AST-grep call-structure artifact was generated."
          },
          "locations": [
